<DOCTMPL oid='767FFCAC2708425e8E462B76A4CC1223' saveno='1'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Vector Reference</TUV>
</NAME>
<QUAL>Vector_Reference</QUAL>
<LABEL>14.1.2</LABEL>
</DOCTMPL>
<RECORDTMPLS>
<RECORDTMPL spec='faultMemory'>
<CVALUETYPE bl='24' bo='21' enc='uns' sig='0' df='hex' qty='atom' sz='no' minsz='0' maxsz='255'/>
<PVALUETYPE bl='16' bo='21' enc='utf' sig='0' df='text' qty='field' sz='no' minsz='0' maxsz='65535'/>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000285C90BF5F0' oid='EC88AF31498D419fB4088204530A483C' temploid='274F054FE4D547b6B305F28F7481A238' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Errortext shortname</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(DEM) Specify DemDTCClass.ShortName and DemEventClass.ShortName for MICROSAR ECU-C.
Blanks will be replaced by underscore.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>DTC_SHORTNAME</QUAL>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000285C90BE6F0' oid='5CDD20D860B34753835095676D29B4FF' temploid='{9DF7F4E6-EFE5-4c11-8BB7-84942DD6CD7C}' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Set Condition</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(Implementation, DiVa, Tester)
How to implement the monitor (pre-failed / failed condition).
Parsed by CANoe.DiVa for a signal name.
Info for After Sales tester which cause might have set the DTC.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>SetCondition</QUAL>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000285C90BC7F0' oid='E5A06EFB6FDA4d9f95E369866F174CD5' temploid='{0D1B721A-9F64-4e0a-A195-EFA82B571130}' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Reset condition &#38; self healing</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(Implementation, DiVa, Tester)
How to implement the monitor (pre-passed / passed condition).
Parsed by CANoe.DiVa for a signal name.
Info for After Sales tester which cause might have reset the DTC.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>ResetCondition</QUAL>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
<UNSRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000285C9265740' oid='9E0A6E7069354b4899CD50B2D418C047' temploid='B2D249520EA848fe961B1D8E08EABA93' mayBeDup='1' conv='req' df='dec' v='2'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>DTC Priority</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(DEM) This value influences the event displacement in case the respective memory is completely filled at the time of event confirmation. 
A lower number represents higher priority (default: 2. Use 1 for OBD)
Specifies DemEventClass.DemEventPriority.
(ref. to Dem104)</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>DTC_PRIORITY_VALUE</QUAL>
</UNSRECORDITEMTMPL>
<ENUMRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000285C8D4F6D0' oid='66404E3BBE2D4e7fA254F97636C28192' temploid='B8F9CF0AF6C94319A1B6BEA3DB0D2685' mayBeDup='1' conv='req' v='0' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Aging Supported</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(DEM) If this parameter is supported, the aging mechanism is enabled for this DTC.
Aging means that the DTC will be automatically removed from fault memory
if the monitor function was executed
and no failure was detected for a configurable number of operation cycles.
The default aging behaviour is MICROSAR value DEM_AGING_TYPE_1.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>DTC_AGING_SUPPORTED</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>supported</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>not supported</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMRECORDITEMTMPL>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000285C90BE2F0' oid='C538E6777C0A4333BD1CA7958ADEAE04' temploid='6AD0EF32419D474d9C5FCD2805DB22ED' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Aging Cycle</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(DEM) Operation cycle name that triggers the aging of this DTC.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>DTC_AGING_CYCLE</QUAL>
<DEFAULT>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>DEM_POWER</TUV>
</DEFAULT>
<CHOICE>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>DEM_IGNITION</TUV>
</CHOICE>
<CHOICE>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>DEM_OBD_DCY</TUV>
</CHOICE>
<CHOICE>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>DEM_WARMUP</TUV>
</CHOICE>
<CHOICE>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>DEM_POWER</TUV>
</CHOICE>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
<UNSRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000285C9265B80' oid='939A0BFBF981403299603F05DC604408' temploid='DC54ED8C244C4d53BDB7B82283D8EAEC' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt' df='dec' v='0'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Aging Cycle Counter Threshold</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(DEM) Number of aging cycles needed to unlearn/delete this DTC.
This parameter has only effect if “Aging supported“ is set to “supported”.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>DTC_AGING_COUNTER</QUAL>
</UNSRECORDITEMTMPL>
<ENUMRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000285C8D4F800' oid='D7997B1C1B1E4d508761A6B37803C89F' temploid='C827388C8C574143ACBBABFBDDAE2D07' mayBeDup='1' conv='req' v='0' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>DTC Severity</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(DEM, Tester) Reports the recommended action to be taken by the system (e.g. vehicle) operator
This parameter is reported by UDS service $19 09 and can serve as a filter for UDS service $19 08.
A missing configuration value (or parameter) is interpreted as noSeverity.
Specifies DemDTCClass.DemDTCSeverity; no further influence on the function of the DEM.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>DTC_SEVERITY_VALUE</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>noSeverity</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='32'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>maintenanceOnly</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='64'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>checkAtNextHalt</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='128'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>checkImmediately</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMRECORDITEMTMPL>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000285C90BD5F0' oid='5DFA5CC0BB5D4db48379022C4B6800EF' temploid='2CA0107F145D487a8C308DA165E0FF06' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Monitor Initialization Function</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(DEM) Values "required", "not required" (select from list).
Describes whether a monitor initialization function is required for events of the DTC.
For value “required”, an initialization function ‘InitMonitorForEvent’ is created (DemEventParameter/DemCallbackInitMForE).
The DEM will call this function each time the event is cleared, or the operation (monitoring) cycle restarts.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>DTC_INIT_MONITOR_REQUIRED</QUAL>
<DEFAULT>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>not required</TUV>
</DEFAULT>
<CHOICE>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>required</TUV>
</CHOICE>
<CHOICE>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>not required</TUV>
</CHOICE>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
<UNSRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000285C92673F0' oid='602551BB94324e6d98C1CD8C9E090B98' temploid='9337448C222E485999CA41EE266FAAE0' mayBeDup='1' conv='req' df='hex' v='0'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Functional Unit</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(DEM, Tester) For use with UDS 19 08 and 19 09 only.
Identifies the corresponding basic vehicle / system function which monitors this DTC.
The default value is 0, use 0x33 for WWH-OBD.
This parameter is necessary for reporting severity information.
It will be returned in the UDS services $19 08 and  $19 09.
If these services are not used, this parameter serves no use at all.
Specifies DemDTCClass.DemDTCFunctionalUnit; no further influence on the function of the DEM.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>DTC_FUNCTIONAL_UNIT_VALUE</QUAL>
</UNSRECORDITEMTMPL>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000285C90BDBF0' oid='6A5D1A4B372D46caB62276A5977C9676' temploid='{99240899-F037-4d89-883E-ED655942A979}' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Repair Instruction</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(Tester) Repair instructions (free text).</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Repair_Instruction</QUAL>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
</RECORDTMPL>
<RECORDTMPL spec='obdFaultMemory'>
<CVALUETYPE bl='16' bo='21' enc='uns' sig='0' df='hex' qty='atom' sz='no' minsz='0' maxsz='255'/>
<PVALUETYPE bl='16' bo='21' enc='utf' sig='0' df='text' qty='field' sz='no' minsz='0' maxsz='65535'/>
<TRRECORDITEMTMPL id='_00000285C90BD6F0' oid='C38AC541BD264691BEC574AB0B03DA3F' temploid='373416C5435B4225A27DB3151EBDB4E1' mayBeDup='1' conv='opt'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>UDS DTC Reference</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Defines the UDS DTC which shall be linked to the OBD DTC. It is also possible to link several UDS DTCs to one single OBD DTC.
The supported format is as follows:
- 3 Byte Hexadecimal DTC number [0x123456 | 123456]
- If more than one DTC is entered separate them with a comma (",")</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>UDS_DTC_Reference</QUAL>
</TRRECORDITEMTMPL>
</RECORDTMPL>
</RECORDTMPLS>
